  "workflows": {},
  "implementation_policy": "Exact event-driven 1D constrained rigid contacts and Coulomb ice friction. Only world X translation is allowed, as requested. Impacts are solved from geometry and current state; no authored event times or pose paths. No unconstrained curling, spin or deformation claim. Visuals keep the handle and cap of the registered Sketchfab Curling Stone by FilinMX, CC BY-NC 4.0, with a granite body lathed from its measured profile and procedural granite and polymer. The club is full 3D geometry in a closed room with scanned CC0 surfaces and props; glossy pebbled ice, its wear map and all optical detail leave collision geometry and frozen rigid motion unchanged.",
